From b2f98a6a81d12e3355531535c493f344ebd3ba37 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: adbtrr_work8_fin_tc <adbtrr_work8_fin_tc@local>
Date: Tue, 8 Sep 2026 06:22:29 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 9/9] os/kernel/log_dump: Add ASSERT hitting test case for
 log_dump_tobuffer

log_dump_tobuffer() appends a compressed character to the tail chunk of
the log dump queue. log_dump_init() always leaves one chunk queued and
log_dump_mem_check() never drops the last one, so the queue is never
empty while the log dump runs. ASSERT(log_dump_tail) catches the
corrupted case before the NULL chunk is written to.

log_dump_tobuffer() is static and works on file scope state, so add
log_dump_tobuffer_asserttest() next to it, built only when the test case
is enabled. It releases every queued chunk and then appends one
character to the tail which is no longer there.

 - os/kernel/log_dump/log_dump.c : test only entry point for the static
   buffer append path.
 - os/include/tinyara/log_dump/log_dump.h : declaration of the entry
   point.
 - os/drivers/os_api_test/kernel/test_assert_log_dump.c : kernel side
   helper reached through the TESTIOC_ASSERT_LOG_DUMP ioctl.
 - apps/examples/testcase/le_tc/kernel/tc_assert_log_dump.c : user side
   test case. A return from the ioctl is a test case failure.

Controlled by CONFIG_TC_KERNEL_ASSERT_LOG_DUMP, default n, depends on
CONFIG_LOG_DUMP. The assertion is an ASSERT(), so CONFIG_DEBUG is not
required. It crashes the board by design and must be enabled alone.
